# Monitoring

## Mục tiêu

Monitoring là window vào health và behavior của production systems. Không có monitoring, teams operate blind - không biết systems đang hoạt động tốt hay đang gặp vấn đề cho đến khi users report. Trong Cursor Enterprise Framework, monitoring không chỉ là watching dashboards mà là một comprehensive observability strategy bao gồm logs, metrics, traces, và alerts. Mục tiêu là enable proactive identification of issues, faster debugging, và data-driven operational decisions.

Observability goes beyond traditional monitoring. Nó cho phép understanding internal states từ external outputs, enabling debugging of issues that were never anticipated. Các systems ngày nay quá phức tạp để predict all possible failure modes, vì vậy observability là essential.

## Nguyên tắc

**1. Three Pillars of Observability**

Logs, metrics, và traces là ba pillars của observability. Logs cung cấp discrete events. Metrics cung cấp aggregated measurements. Traces cung cấp request flow across services. All three are needed for complete observability. Each serves different debugging scenarios.

**2. Structured Logging**

Use structured logging format (JSON) for machine parsing. Include consistent fields in every log entry. Log levels: ERROR, WARN, INFO, DEBUG. Never log sensitive data. Include correlation IDs for request tracing. Structured logs enable efficient searching và filtering.

**3. Metrics-Driven Culture**

Define SLIs (Service Level Indicators) và SLOs (Service Level Objectives). Track metrics consistently across services. Use RED method: Rate, Errors, Duration. Use USE method: Utilization, Saturation, Errors. Make metrics actionable, not just informational.

**4. Distributed Tracing**

Trace requests across all services. Use correlation IDs consistently. Sample traces intelligently (not 100%). Include span attributes for context. Trace libraries: OpenTelemetry, Jaeger, Zipkin. Distributed tracing essential for microservices debugging.

**5. Alert on Symptoms, Not Causes**

Alert on user-impacting symptoms. Too many alerts cause alert fatigue. Use composite alerts to reduce noise. Alert on trends, not just thresholds. Page only for actionable items. Document alert response procedures.

**6. Service Level Objectives**

Define SLOs for every critical service. SLOs should reflect user expectations. Track SLO compliance over time. Error budgets for release decisions. SLO breaches trigger investigation. Share SLO status with stakeholders.

**7. Health Checks**

Implement health check endpoints. Check dependency health, not just process. Include checks for external dependencies. Health checks should be fast (<1s). Separate readiness và liveness checks. Use health checks for load balancing.

**8. Dashboard Design**

Dashboards should tell a story. Start with high-level overview. Drill down to details on demand. Use consistent time ranges. Include annotations for deployments. Remove noise, focus on signal.

**9. Cost of Monitoring**

Monitoring infrastructure has cost. Balance granularity vs cost. Sample data when full fidelity not needed. Use metric aggregation wisely. Right-size retention policies. Monitor the monitors themselves.

**10. Runbooks**

Every alert should have a runbook. Runbooks document how to respond. Include escalation paths. Keep runbooks up to date. Practice incident response. Runbooks reduce MTTR (Mean Time To Recovery).

## Checklist

- [ ] Logging framework configured
- [ ] Structured logging implemented
- [ ] Metrics collection setup
- [ ] Distributed tracing configured
- [ ] Health checks implemented
- [ ] SLOs defined for critical services
- [ ] Alerts configured with runbooks
- [ ] Dashboards created
- [ ] On-call rotation established
- [ ] Incident response process documented
- [ ] Monitoring costs tracked
- [ ] Regular monitoring reviews scheduled

## Anti Pattern

**1. No Monitoring**

Deploying without monitoring infrastructure. Operating in darkness. Issues discovered by users, not team. No data for troubleshooting. This is unacceptable for production systems.

**2. Too Many Alerts**

Hundreds of alerts firing constantly. Alert fatigue sets in. Critical alerts ignored. Focus on actionable, high-impact alerts. Quality over quantity.

**3. Logging Everything**

Massive log volumes without value. Storage costs explode. Signal-to-noise ratio poor. Log strategically, not exhaustively. Focus on decision-supporting data.

**4. Dashboard Zoo**

Hundreds of meaningless dashboards. No one looks at them. Dashboards not telling stories. Create dashboards with purpose. Review và prune regularly.

**5. Alerts Without Context**

Alert fires without explanation. Responder doesn't know what to do. Every alert needs context. Include relevant links và runbooks. Make alerts actionable.

## Best Practice

**1. Structured Logging Implementation**

```typescript
// Structured logger interface
interface LogEntry {
  timestamp: string;
  level: 'DEBUG' | 'INFO' | 'WARN' | 'ERROR';
  message: string;
  service: string;
  environment: string;
  version: string;
  correlationId?: string;
  userId?: string;
  requestId?: string;
  duration?: number;
  error?: {
    name: string;
    message: string;
    stack?: string;
  };
  metadata?: Record<string, any>;
}

class StructuredLogger {
  constructor(
    private config: LoggerConfig,
    private transport: LogTransport
  ) {}
  
  private formatEntry(entry: Partial<LogEntry>): LogEntry {
    return {
      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
      level: entry.level || 'INFO',
      service: this.config.serviceName,
      environment: this.config.environment,
      version: this.config.version,
      message: entry.message || '',
      ...entry
    };
  }
  
  info(message: string, metadata?: Record<string, any>) {
    this.log('INFO', message, metadata);
  }
  
  error(message: string, error?: Error, metadata?: Record<string, any>) {
    this.log('ERROR', message, {
      ...metadata,
      error: error ? {
        name: error.name,
        message: error.message,
        stack: error.stack
      } : undefined
    });
  }
  
  private log(
    level: LogEntry['level'],
    message: string,
    metadata?: Record<string, any>
  ) {
    const entry = this.formatEntry({ level, message, metadata });
    
    // Console output in development
    if (this.config.environment === 'development') {
      console.log(JSON.stringify(entry, null, 2));
    }
    
    // Send to transport
    this.transport.send(entry);
  }
}

// Request logging middleware
class RequestLoggingMiddleware {
  constructor(private logger: StructuredLogger) {}
  
  handler() {
    return async (request: Request, response: Response, next: NextFunction) => {
      const startTime = Date.now();
      const correlationId = request.headers['x-correlation-id'] as string || 
        generateUUID();
      
      request.correlationId = correlationId;
      response.setHeader('X-Correlation-ID', correlationId);
      
      // Log request
      this.logger.info('Request started', {
        correlationId,
        method: request.method,
        path: request.path,
        query: request.query,
        userAgent: request.headers['user-agent']
      });
      
      // Capture response
      const originalEnd = response.end;
      response.end = function(...args: any[]) {
        const duration = Date.now() - startTime;
        
        logger.log(response.statusCode >= 400 ? 'ERROR' : 'INFO', 'Request completed', {
          correlationId,
          method: request.method,
          path: request.path,
          statusCode: response.statusCode,
          duration,
          userId: request.user?.id
        });
        
        return originalEnd.apply(this, args);
      };
      
      next();
    };
  }
}
```

**2. Metrics Collection with Prometheus**

```typescript
// Metrics definitions
const metrics = {
  httpRequestsTotal: new Counter({
    name: 'http_requests_total',
    help: 'Total HTTP requests',
    labelNames: ['method', 'path', 'status']
  }),
  
  httpRequestDuration: new Histogram({
    name: 'http_request_duration_seconds',
    help: 'HTTP request duration',
    labelNames: ['method', 'path'],
    buckets: [0.01, 0.05, 0.1, 0.5, 1, 5]
  }),
  
  activeConnections: new Gauge({
    name: 'active_connections',
    help: 'Number of active connections',
    labelNames: ['type']
  }),
  
  queueDepth: new Gauge({
    name: 'queue_depth',
    help: 'Current queue depth',
    labelNames: ['queue_name']
  }),
  
  cacheHitRate: new Gauge({
    name: 'cache_hit_rate',
    help: 'Cache hit rate',
    labelNames: ['cache_name']
  })
};

// Metrics middleware
class MetricsMiddleware {
  constructor(private metrics: MetricsRegistry) {}
  
  handler() {
    return async (request: Request, response: Response, next: NextFunction) => {
      const startTime = Date.now();
      
      // Normalize path to prevent cardinality explosion
      const normalizedPath = this.normalizePath(request.path);
      
      this.metrics.httpRequestsTotal.inc({
        method: request.method,
        path: normalizedPath,
        status: 'pending'
      });
      
      const originalEnd = response.end;
      response.end = function(...args: any[]) {
        const duration = (Date.now() - startTime) / 1000;
        
        metrics.httpRequestsTotal.inc({
          method: request.method,
          path: normalizedPath,
          status: response.statusCode
        });
        
        metrics.httpRequestDuration.observe(
          { method: request.method, path: normalizedPath },
          duration
        );
        
        return originalEnd.apply(this, args);
      };
      
      next();
    };
  }
  
  private normalizePath(path: string): string {
    // Replace UUIDs
    path = path.replace(
      /[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}/gi,
      ':id'
    );
    
    // Replace numeric IDs
    path = path.replace(/\/\d+/g, '/:id');
    
    return path;
  }
}

// Business metrics
class OrderMetrics {
  constructor(private metrics: MetricsRegistry) {}
  
  recordOrderCreated(order: Order) {
    this.metrics.orderTotal.inc({
      status: 'created',
      currency: order.currency
    });
  }
  
  recordOrderCompleted(order: Order) {
    this.metrics.orderTotal.inc({
      status: 'completed',
      currency: order.currency
    });
    
    this.metrics.orderValue.observe(
      order.total
    );
  }
  
  recordPaymentFailed(error: PaymentError) {
    this.metrics.paymentErrors.inc({
      errorType: error.type
    });
  }
}
```

**3. Distributed Tracing with OpenTelemetry**

```typescript
// OpenTelemetry setup
import { NodeSDK } from '@opentelemetry/sdk-node';
import { JaegerExporter } from '@opentelemetry/exporter-jaeger';
import { HttpInstrumentation } from '@opentelemetry/instrumentation-http';
import { ExpressInstrumentation } from '@opentelemetry/instrumentation-express';
import { PrismaInstrumentation } from '@opentelemetry/instrumentation-prisma';
import { RedisInstrumentation } from '@opentelemetry/instrumentation-redis';

const sdk = new NodeSDK({
  serviceName: 'order-service',
  traceExporter: new JaegerExporter({
    endpoint: 'http://jaeger:14268/api/traces'
  }),
  instrumentations: [
    new HttpInstrumentation(),
    new ExpressInstrumentation(),
    new PrismaInstrumentation(),
    new RedisInstrumentation()
  ]
});

sdk.start();

// Custom span creation
class TracingService {
  constructor(
    private tracer: Tracer,
    private metrics: MetricsRegistry
  ) {}
  
  async traceOperation<T>(
    operationName: string,
    attributes: Record<string, string>,
    operation: (span: Span) => Promise<T>
  ): Promise<T> {
    return this.tracer.startActiveSpan(operationName, async (span) => {
      try {
        // Set attributes
        Object.entries(attributes).forEach(([key, value]) => {
          span.setAttribute(key, value);
        });
        
        // Add to metrics
        const startTime = Date.now();
        
        const result = await operation(span);
        
        // Record success
        span.setStatus({ code: SpanStatusCode.OK });
        this.metrics.operationDuration.observe(
          { operation: operationName },
          (Date.now() - startTime) / 1000
        );
        
        return result;
      } catch (error) {
        // Record error
        span.setStatus({
          code: SpanStatusCode.ERROR,
          message: error.message
        });
        span.recordException(error as Error);
        
        this.metrics.operationErrors.inc({
          operation: operationName,
          errorType: (error as Error).name
        });
        
        throw error;
      } finally {
        span.end();
      }
    });
  }
  
  async traceDatabaseQuery<T>(
    query: string,
    operation: () => Promise<T>
  ): Promise<T> {
    return this.traceOperation(
      `db.query.${this.normalizeQueryName(query)}`,
      { 'db.statement': query },
      operation
    );
  }
  
  private normalizeQueryName(query: string): string {
    // Extract operation type
    const match = query.match(/^\s*(SELECT|INSERT|UPDATE|DELETE)/i);
    return match ? match[1].toLowerCase() : 'unknown';
  }
}
```

